name duel-merge-1
timeout 300

# THE ASYMMETRIC DUEL, GEOMETRY 6: THE MERGE — the one place the MiG-29's weapon set is not the
# inferior one, and therefore the mission that has to exist before the campaign may claim the F-16
# dominates. The four BVR geometries all turn on radar reach and Rtr, and on both the MiG is behind by
# construction (2.0x and 1.7x, measured). Inside the merge neither matters: an R-73 is cued off the
# helmet, a GSh-301 round carries 2.7x the energy of an M61A1 round, and the airframe out-turns and
# out-rolls the F-16 (measured corner 420 kt / 24.2 deg/s against 380 / 16.2; roll plant 201 deg/s per
# full deflection against 78.7).
#
# THE SETUP: 8 km apart, head-on, co-altitude, both on `set task bfm` — the close-combat control law
# on both sides, no BVR phase and no long shot. Both start inside every launch zone either side has.
#
# THE MiG ACQUIRES IN THE MERGE (prior round). The pilot switches the N019 to ACM in the fight phase
# (pilot/FBPilot::BfmSelectRadarMode + FBMig29Pilot::BfmRadarModeOrdinal = the broad forward auto-lock
# volume FBMig29Radar::kAcm*, +-37 deg az from T4 7.1 read as azimuth, a +-30 deg vertical band,
# Doppler-exempt like CC), so the auto-lock does the designation the earlier RAD bar could never make.
# The narrow RAD/CC/VS/BORE pencils are unchanged and still used elsewhere (mig29-r73). The F-16 is in
# ACM HUD as before.
#
# AND THE F-16 NOW SURVIVES IT (this round). Its BFM roll law had a PEAK rate cap (90 deg/s) and no bound
# on how LONG a roll may last, while the judge's rule is a SUSTAINED rate (|w| > 60 deg/s for 3 s). At
# 898 kt of closure the line of sight sweeps at up to 543 deg/s -- 34x the corner turn rate -- so the
# commanded lift direction rotated WITH the aircraft, the roll error never closed and the law rolled
# 290 deg in 3.1 s on a 10-20 deg steering error. The same 180 deg that gives the peak cap now also bounds
# the roll flown per kBfmTurnTimeS (doc/pilot.md 5.7.3); the sustained rate follows as cap/2.
#
# AND THE MiG NOW SURVIVES IT TOO (this round), which is why the exit code moved 2 -> 3. It used to fly
# into the ground at t=232.3 out of a lost-contact turn, and the cause was NOT the pilot and NOT the
# floor: systems/FBFlightControl applied this airframe's own rate DAMPER (KqDamp/KpDampRoll -- the
# SAU-451 "DAMPER", doc/modules/mig29/flight-model-spec.md 7.4 names it "FBFlightControl's inner rate
# loop") only on its FLCS path, and BFM commands Manual. The jet fought every merge with the damper off.
# Measured in isolation, one MiG alone in a cold BFM search, 300 s: mean g command 4.57, mean bank
# 76 deg, p95 |VS| 183 m/s, CFIT from all three start altitudes -- against 1.11 / 24 deg / 4 m/s and no
# KO with the damper, and 1.22 / 40 deg / 9 m/s for the F-16 flying the identical search.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 (TIMEOUT), and the verdict is the telemetry. Measured this round:
#   NO monitor KO on either side, the run goes to its full 300 s (was 232.3).
#   VIPER (F-16): lock_s 28.2 -> 47.6, min AGL 449 -> 4487 m. It no longer settles below its own
#     2000 ft BFM floor, because the fight no longer spirals down.
#   FULCRUM (MiG): RADAR_LOCK t=3.8 (3.31 nm) unchanged, lock_s 79.4 -> 70.6, min AGL -4 -> 4548 m,
#     and it still gets a GSh-301 burst away (24 rounds over two triggers), which still misses.
# WHAT THIS RUN MEASURES, and it is STILL NOT the weapon thesis: the viper spends 231.6 of 300.1 s with
# bfm_rng = -1, the fulcrum 223.7 s, 220.1 s both at once -- worse as a FRACTION than before (73 %
# against 82 % for the viper, 75 % against 62 % for the fulcrum), because the two jets now climb away
# from each other instead of sinking together. After the first pass neither ACM box re-acquires. So the
# R-73/GSh-301 thesis stays untested for a FIFTH reason, and it is again the honest one: the pilots
# cannot hold each other in a knife fight. The blocker is close-combat re-acquisition -- the floor and
# the airframe are both off the list. doc/duels.md D1, doc/pilot.md gaps 2.9 + 2.8.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.95000 5000 90.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud                      # auto-locks the nearest firm track: no thumb needed
  set fcr_range_nm 10
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 7.20000 5000 380
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.05500 5000 270.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode rad                         # BVR default; the BFM pilot switches to ACM in the fight
  set n019_range_nm 10
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r73
  set store 4 r73
  set cmds_mode man                          # the MiG can now defend too (BVP-30-26, this round)
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 6.80000 5000 380
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive
